<title>ITALY: Visco says scope for rate cuts now lira in ERM.</title>
<headline>Visco says scope for rate cuts now lira in ERM.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Finance Minister Vincenzo Visco said that the return of the lira to the European currency grid opens up prospects of further cuts in interest rates including the Bank of Italy's key discount rate.</p>
<p>&quot;Yesterday's decision will result in further reductions in interest rates and in the discount rate,&quot; Visco told reporters as he entered an upper house Senate budget commission meeting to discuss the 1997 budget bill.  </p>
<p>Visco added that now that the lira was back in the exchange rate mechanism with a central parity of 990 per mark, &quot;our economy will have a stable anchorage in Europe. There will be a more solid and less uncertain recovery.&quot;</p>
</text>
